  "profile": {
    "video_id": "iron-snail:0ZLO5gHDneY",
    "purpose": "A first-impressions review and buying guide for the Barbour Bedale waxed jacket. It covers model choice, sizing, the difference between Sylkoil and thornproof wax finishes, the jacket's features, patina, and a shower water-resistance test.",
    "video_type": "review",
    "thesis": "The creator walks through his first Barbour, the classic Bedale, explaining what a buyer needs to know about fit, finish types, details and how water resistant a waxed jacket really is.",
    "key_takeaways": [
      "The creator chose the regular-cut Bedale over the slimmer, more modern Ashby, wanting room for layers and long-term wear.",
      "He sized down from his usual 38 to a 36 and suggests sizing down one if you can't try it on in person.",
      "Sylkoil uses uncombed cotton that looks fuzzier as the wax wears, while thornproof uses combed and calendered cotton that is smoother and glassier.",
      "The calendering process presses the weave tighter, which he says adds wind and water resistance and lets thorns slide off instead of snagging.",
      "The video covers the jacket's details: zipper bottle opener, snap-on hood, tartan lining, zip-in liner, knit storm cuffs, storm flap, throat latch, corduroy collar and moleskin-lined handwarmer pockets.",
      "Barbour has a repair program for damaged jackets.",
      "Patina is a trade-off: worn areas look good but have less wax, so they are less water resistant.",
      "In a shower test the freshly waxed jacket did not leak; he stresses it is water resistant rather than waterproof and depends on upkeep.",
      "According to the creator, Barbour's own re-wax product is used for both finishes."
    ],
    "outline": [
      {
        "title": "Introduction to the hike",
        "summary": "Michael opens on a fall hike, introduces his first Barbour and previews the topics: Sylkoil vs thornproof, the water test, fit, model choice and details.",
