        "last_segment": 1
      },
      {
        "title": "First Barbour jacket",
        "summary": "Why he picked the classic Bedale in regular cut over the slimmer Ashby, including trying both on over a flannel and sweater. Also covers the Barbour pin and the jacket's British and ivy/prep connotations.",
        "first_segment": 1,
        "last_segment": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "Sizing and fit guide",
        "summary": "His sizing (a 36 instead of his usual 38) and the advice to size down one when buying without trying on.",
        "first_segment": 2,
        "last_segment": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Waxed finish comparison",
        "summary": "Explains Sylkoil versus thornproof finishes, using a fisherman sweater vs glass pane analogy. Covers uncombed versus combed and calendered cotton, and the resulting wind and water resistance; he notes he couldn't confirm whether the factory wax blends differ.",
        "first_segment": 3,
        "last_segment": 7
      },
      {
        "title": "Jacket details and features",
        "summary": "A rundown of the Bedale's features, from the bottle-opener zipper to the hood, lining, cuffs, flap, collar and pockets, plus Barbour's repair program. Ends with the patina versus water resistance catch-22.",
        "first_segment": 7,
        "last_segment": 11
      },
      {
        "title": "Water resistance test",
        "summary": "A shower test of the new jacket, which didn't leak, and a discussion of how water resistance depends on the state of the wax. Includes an anecdote about oilskins failing in storms.",
        "first_segment": 11,
        "last_segment": 13
      }
    ],
